---
component: lampLighting
params:
  # Whoever keeps the light now. The glass follows the host's weather unless a
  # ::use says otherwise (dsl 0.26.0 §3.3: a default is a literal or a host @def).
  keeper: { type: string, default: "The inspector" }
  glass: { type: { enum: [steady, guttering] }, default: "@glassTonight" }
---

## Lighting the Lamp

::sfx{sound="brass_crank"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: {{@keeper}} climbs the hundred and eleven steps, trims the wick, and sets the clockwork turning.
<match on="@glass">
  <when is="steady">
    @narrator{code="0020"}: The beam walks out across the water, steady as a heartbeat. Five seconds dark, one second bright.
  </when>
  <when is="guttering">
    @narrator{code="0030"}: The wind finds every seam in the lantern. The flame leans and gutters, and the beam stutters over the Teeth.
  </when>
</match>
